## SLO

<!-- bench-report:begin slo -->
<!-- Generated by `bench report --out docs/03-results.md results/a results/b results/c` from docs/slo.json. Edit outside the markers only. -->

| Profile | A level meets the SLO when | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| `interactive` | TTFT p95 ≤ 100 ms and TPOT p95 ≤ 25 ms, with no errors | test |
| `throughput` | E2E p95 ≤ 15 s, with no errors | test |

<!-- bench-report:end slo -->

## interactive

<!-- bench-report:begin headline:interactive -->
<!-- Generated by `bench report --out docs/03-results.md results/a results/b results/c` from results/interactive-baseline-20260101-000000, results/interactive-batching-20260101-010000, docs/slo.json. Edit outside the markers only. -->

| Run | Engine config | SLO | Max compliant goodput (tok/s) | At c | Next level up |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `interactive-baseline-20260101-000000` | `baseline` | TTFT p95 ≤ 100 ms and TPOT p95 ≤ 25 ms | 200.0 | 2 | c=4, 380.0 tok/s: fails TTFT p95 117.1 ms (+17.1%), fails TPOT p95 26.3 ms (+5.2%) |
| `interactive-batching-20260101-010000` | `batching` | TTFT p95 ≤ 100 ms and TPOT p95 ≤ 25 ms | 400.0 | 4 | c=8, 600.0 tok/s: fails TTFT p95 150.0 ms (+50.0%), fails TPOT p95 30.0 ms (+20.0%) |

Max compliant goodput is the highest output tok/s among the levels that meet the SLO and pass the engine check; a tie goes to the lower concurrency.

<!-- bench-report:end headline:interactive -->

### interactive-baseline-20260101-000000

<!-- bench-report:begin table:interactive-baseline-20260101-000000 -->
<!-- Generated by `bench report --out docs/03-results.md results/a results/b results/c` from results/interactive-baseline-20260101-000000, docs/slo.json. Edit outside the markers only. -->

Run `interactive-baseline-20260101-000000`: profile `interactive`, engine config `baseline`, 10 s warmup and 10 s measured window per level.

| c | Requests | Errors | RPS | Output tok/s | TTFT p50 | TTFT p95 | TTFT p99 | TPOT p50 | TPOT p95 | TPOT p99 | E2E p50 | E2E p95 | E2E p99 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | 1 | 0 | 0.10 | 100.0 | 9.2 | 18.4 | 19.4 | 4.8 | 9.5 | 10.5 | 1.00 | 2.00 | 3.00 |
| 2 | 1 | 0 | 0.10 | 200.0 | 16.0 | 32.0 | 33.0 | 4.8 | 9.7 | 10.7 | 1.00 | 2.00 | 3.00 |
| 4 | 1 | 0 | 0.10 | 380.0 | 58.5 | 117.1 | 118.1 | 13.2 | 26.3 | 27.3 | 1.00 | 2.00 | 3.00 |

TTFT and TPOT in ms, E2E in s: nearest-rank percentiles over each level's successful requests (TPOT excludes completion_tokens < 2). RPS and output tok/s count successful requests over the measured window.

| c | TTFT p95 ≤ 100 ms | TPOT p95 ≤ 25 ms | Meets SLO | Engine check | Output tok/s | Requests meeting SLO | Per-request goodput (tok/s) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | pass 18.4 ms (-81.6%) | pass 9.5 ms (-62.0%) | yes | ok | 100.0 | 1 / 1 (100.0%) | 100.0 |
| 2 | pass 32.0 ms (-68.0%) | pass 9.7 ms (-61.2%) | yes | ok | 200.0 | 1 / 1 (100.0%) | 200.0 |
| 4 | **FAIL** 117.1 ms (+17.1%) | **FAIL** 26.3 ms (+5.2%) | no | ok | 380.0 | 1 / 1 (100.0%) | 380.0 |

A level meets the SLO when every bound holds (a value equal to the limit passes) and it had no errors; the margin is (value − limit) / limit. Per-request goodput counts the output tokens of the requests that each met every limit on their own, per second of the measured window. The engine check is the uncached-prompt guard in the engine table.

<!-- bench-report:end table:interactive-baseline-20260101-000000 -->

